WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.914
Hi! Before we find the area of a triangle, we need to know its base and its height.

2
00:00:08.064 --> 00:00:13.530
Any side of a triangle can be the base. Let's choose AB as the base.

3
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.242
The height is the line from the opposite corner, C, that meets the base at a right angle.

4
00:00:19.392 --> 00:00:25.986
If we choose BC as the base instead, the height starts from A and goes to BC at a right angle.

5
00:00:26.136 --> 00:00:34.074
If CA is the base, the height starts from B. So a triangle has three pairs of base and height!

6
00:00:34.224 --> 00:00:41.562
A right-angled triangle is special. The two sides that form the right angle are a base and a height for each other.

7
00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:51.066
For an obtuse-angled triangle, the height can be outside. We extend the base, then draw the height from the corner at a right angle.

8
00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:56.826
Let's try this one. The base is BC. Which line is the height?

9
00:00:56.976 --> 00:01:03.690
AB and AC are slanted. They don't meet BC at a right angle, so they are not the height.

10
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:11.586
AD starts at corner A and meets BC at a right angle. So AD is the height.

11
00:01:11.736 --> 00:01:18.066
One more: in obtuse-angled triangle PQR, the base is QR. Where is the height?

12
00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:24.066
A line straight down from P lands outside the triangle, so first we extend QR.

13
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:31.026
PS meets the extended line QR at a right angle, so PS is the height.

14
00:01:31.176 --> 00:01:37.698
Watch out! Some pupils think any line that looks upright is the height. That is wrong!

15
00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:44.658
The height must be at a right angle to the base you chose. If the base changes, the height changes too.

16
00:01:44.808 --> 00:01:52.746
First find the base, then look for the line that is perpendicular to it. Check for the right-angle mark.

17
00:01:52.896 --> 00:02:05.994
Your turn! In right-angled triangle PQR, angle Q is a right angle. If the base is QR, which side is the height? Pause and think.

18
00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:13.578
The answer is PQ, because PQ meets QR at a right angle. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:13.728 --> 00:02:26.466
Another one! In triangle ABC, AD is perpendicular to BC. AD is the height for which base? Pause and think.

20
00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:35.058
AD meets BC at a right angle, so AD is the height for base BC. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:46.794
Last one! In a right-angled triangle, if one side of the right angle is the base, which line is the height? Pause and think.

22
00:02:46.944 --> 00:02:55.626
The height is the other side of the right angle, because it is already at a right angle to the base. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:55.776 --> 00:03:05.802
Remember: the height goes from a corner to the opposite side and meets the base at a right angle. Every side can be a base, and each base has its own height.

24
00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:10.146
Now go and practise in your garden!

